 ## Overview
-The Voxel Volume Data Format defines a voxel volume as a JSON object containing an `attributes` array, a `position` array, a `size` array, and a `primitives` array [S1, unofficial]. Each attribute specifies a semantic property and its component type, while primitives define sub-volumes with spatial bounds and attribute data [S1, unofficial]. This differs from flat binary list formats like VL32, which store voxels in a continuous struct array without a schema header [S2].
